<%# locals: (showcase:)

    The laptop screen's contest LIVE page, as a static snapshot: what
    /contests/<slug>/live draws for NextContest.live_showcase's contest (the one
    being played, else the one that finished last). The featured game and the
    games strip are the live page's OWN partials (live/_game_tile,
    contests/_live_games) with real data. The featured game is the tile at its
    board size, not :hero: the hero type is set for a full-width row and
    truncates team names in this column.

    A DESKTOP PAGE, SHRUNK. The caller draws this on a 1280px canvas scaled to
    the laptop screen, so it gets desktop layout (Tailwind breakpoints read the
    viewport, which is desktop wherever the laptop shows) and is clipped by the
    screen, never squeezed.

    STATIC. The whole subtree carries x-ignore, so Alpine never walks it: no
    carousel, no polling. It subscribes to nothing (no turbo_stream_from here;
    the live page's streams live in live.html.erb, which is not rendered).

    THE LEADERBOARD IS NOT contests/_turf_totals_leaderboard, deliberately. That
    partial reads current_user (admin controls, "Add 2nd Entry" buttons) and
    draws every empty seat, and it names players with User#display_name, which
    falls back to an EMAIL prefix or a truncated WALLET. On a public marketing
    page none of that may appear, whoever is signed in. So the top entries are
    drawn here from the same rows: rank, the player's chosen username (or
    "Player N" when there is none), and score. The live page is public
    (ContestsController skips authentication for :live), so a username shown
    there is already public. The contest chat is omitted entirely: no message
    body is drawn.

    LAID OUT FOR WHAT SHOWS. The phone covers a small lower-left corner of the
    screen and the hero clips its right side, so the content runs in one
    540px column starting 140px in, which lands wholly in the visible region. %>
<% contest = showcase.contest %>
<div x-ignore class="w-[1280px]" data-test="laptop-live">
  <div class="flex items-center gap-5 border-b border-subtle px-6 py-3">
    <p class="text-xl font-extrabold text-heading">Turf <span class="tm-wordmark">Monster</span></p>
    <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-heading">Contests</p>
    <p class="text-sm text-muted">Rules</p>
  </div>
  <div class="ml-[140px] w-[540px] space-y-4 py-5">
    <div>
      <% if contest.slate %>
        <p class="text-sm text-secondary font-medium"><%= contest.slate.name %></p>
      <% end %>
      <% badge = contest_live_badge(contest) %>
      <p class="text-2xl font-extrabold text-heading flex items-center gap-2 flex-wrap">
        <%= contest.name %>
        <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider <%= badge[:classes] %>">
          <span class="h-2 w-2 rounded-full <%= badge[:dot] %>"></span> <%= badge[:label] %>
        </span>
      </p>
    </div>

    <% focus_game = showcase.games.values.flatten.find { |g| g.slug == showcase.focus_slug } %>
    <% if focus_game %>
      <%= render "live/game_tile", game: focus_game, scorers: true %>
    <% end %>

    <div class="overflow-hidden"><%= render "contests/live_games", **showcase.games, contest: contest %></div>

    <div class="card p-4" data-test="laptop-live-leaderboard">
      <p class="text-sm font-bold text-heading mb-3">Leaderboard</p>
      <% if showcase.leaders.empty? %>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted">No entries yet.</p>
      <% end %>
      <ol class="space-y-2">
        <% showcase.leaders.each_with_index do |entry, i| %>
          <li class="flex items-center gap-3" data-test="laptop-live-leader">
            <span class="w-6 text-center font-mono font-bold text-heading"><%= i + 1 %></span>
            <span class="flex-1 truncate font-semibold text-heading"><%= entry.user&.username.presence || "Player #{i + 1}" %></span>
            <span class="font-mono font-bold text-primary"><%= number_with_precision(entry.score, precision: 1) %></span>
          </li>
        <% end %>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
